// Standard Template Library (STL) 

// STL is used in :
// Competitive Programming !
// It helps to solve problems efficiently.

// What is STL ?
// STL is Stands for standard template library !
// It's a collection of reusable C++ code which provides developers with efficient solutions to common programming tasks.
// Library of what : Generic Classes and functions .

// Why Use STL ?
// While using STL we "Reuse Well Tested Components !"
// We don't have to write our own !
// It saves time & effort.

// Components of STL :
/*
1. Containers - Vector, List, Set, Map, String etc. they use template classes and stores data !
2. Algorithms - set of Functions which perform operations on containers like vector, list or algorithm like sorting , merging etc. They also use Function Templates !
3. Iterators - Point to elements inside a container. They are used with algorithms.
4. Functors - A function object that stores a callable entity such as a function pointer or an object along with an operator() method.
*/